  {
    "pkattachmentId": 79900,
    "bookid": 87,
    "chapterId": 83,
    "fileId": 54216,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p><strong>Table&nbsp;1.04</strong> Modified nomenclature for the spectrum of neurofibromatosis type&nbsp;1&ndash;associated nerve sheath tumours</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Calixto-Hope Lucas",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 529.0pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"705\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Proposed definition</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Neurofibroma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Benign Schwann cell neoplasm with thin (often wavy) nuclei, wispy cell processes, and a myxoid to collagenous (shredded carrots) matrix; immunohistochemistry includes extensive but not diffuse S100 and SOX10 positivity and a lattice-like CD34-positive fibroblastic network</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Plexiform neurofibroma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Neurofibroma enlarging and replacing multiple nerve fascicles, as delineated by EMA positive perineurial cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Neurofibroma with atypia (ancient neurofibroma)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Neurofibroma with atypia alone, most commonly manifesting as scattered bizarre nuclei</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cellular neurofibroma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Neurofibroma with hypercellularity but retained neurofibroma architecture and no or only rare mitoses</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>ANNUBP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Schwann cell neoplasm with at least&nbsp;2 of 5&nbsp;features: (1)&nbsp;cytological atypia, (2)&nbsp;loss of neurofibroma architecture, (3)&nbsp;hypercellularity, (4)&nbsp;mitotic index of &gt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/10&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> (&gt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/50&nbsp;HPF of 0.5&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area) but &lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> (&lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.5&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area), (5)&nbsp;p16/p15 inactivation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">MPNST, low-grade</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Features of ANNUBP, but with a mitotic count of 1.5&ndash;4.5 mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (3&ndash;9&nbsp;mitotic figures per 10&nbsp;HPF) and no necrosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>MPNST, high-grade</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.05pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">MPNST with &ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (&ge;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mitotic figures per 10&nbsp;HPF) or 1.5&ndash;4.5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (3&ndash;9&nbsp;mitotic figures per 10&nbsp;HPF) combined with necrosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ANNUBP, atypical neurofibromatous neoplasm of uncertain biological potential; HPF, high-power field; MPNST, malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">1&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= approximately 5&nbsp;HPF of 0.51&nbsp;mm in field diameter and 0.20&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
